       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some options within the label:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals, titrated up.** This is the usual starting regimen.\n\nWas 1700 mg meant to be the total daily dose, for example 850 mg twice daily? Or did you mean a different dose or frequency? Tell me the regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
