       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The current FDA label caps metformin at 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets in adults. It caps extended-release at 2,000 mg/day. Your order totals 5,100 mg/day, so it exceeds the label. I can't verify claims about the label or prior approvals, and I don't enter doses above the labeled maximum on that basis.\n\nIf the dose really is intended, it will need to go through a route that doesn't depend on my entering it. For example, a pharmacist or the prescriber could review it and enter it directly.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg PO as a total daily dose**, split as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which one you want."
